# Append-biased union merge for memory topic files: on a rebase/merge conflict,
# keep BOTH sides instead of picking one — memory loss is worse than duplication,
# and de-duplication is the MEMORY.md index's job, not git's.
#
# `union` is one of git's BUILT-IN low-level merge drivers, so it needs no
# `merge.<name>.driver` config and works in a fresh clone with zero setup —
# including for someone who runs a plain `git pull --rebase` without ever
# invoking scripts/memory-sync.sh. Do NOT replace it with a custom driver name:
# git silently ignores an unregistered driver and falls back to a normal
# three-way merge, which reintroduces exactly the conflict this line prevents.
*.md merge=union
